    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Title>Log.Assert( A better style of application logging )</Title>
    <PackageDescription><![CDATA[Log.Assert is a better style of application logging.
```
log.Member();                     // logs Method name
log.PreconditionNotNull(target);  // logs nothing if true, or the failure if not.

var graphemes = new StringInfo(target??"");
log.Assert(graphemes.LengthInTextElements > 0); // logs nothing if true, or the failure if not.

log.Precondition(0 <= guess && guess <= graphemes.LengthInTextElements);

if (graphemes.SubstringByTextElements(guess,1) is "💥")
    throw new ApplicationException("bang!");

var remainder = Remove(graphemes,guess);

log.Postcondition(remainder.Length < target.Length);
```
All methods log the current Method or Member name.
Assertions,Pre- and Post-Conditions log nothing at all if they pass
Assertions,Pre- and Post-Conditions log the failed expression if they fail.
LogIf() logs nothing if the condition is false
LogIf() logs the condition expression if it is true

```
Member()
Assert()
Precondition()
Postcondition()

LogIf()
LogDebugIf()
LogTraceIf()
LogWarningIf()
LogErrorIf()
LogExceptionIf()

LogException()
LogExceptionAndThrow()
LogCriticalAndExitProcessWithExitCode()
```
]]></PackageDescription>
